 "phrases": [
  {
   "text": "You take one big gulp of an ice-cold drink,",
   "s": 0.204,
   "e": 2.645
  },
  {
   "text": "and suddenly your forehead explodes.",
   "s": 2.932,
   "e": 4.883
  },
  {
   "text": "That is a brain freeze,",
   "s": 5.43,
   "e": 6.314
  },
  {
   "text": "and it is your brain trying to save itself.",
   "s": 6.713,
   "e": 8.412
  },
  {
   "text": "The cold hits the roof of your mouth,",
   "s": 9.081,
   "e": 10.508
  },
  {
   "text": "where blood vessels sit just under the skin.",
   "s": 10.878,
   "e": 12.689
  },
  {
   "text": "They slam shut to keep the cold out.",
   "s": 13.299,
   "e": 14.88
  },
  {
   "text": "But your brain is picky about temperature.",
   "s": 15.466,
   "e": 17.145
  },
  {
   "text": "It panics and orders warm blood to rush up.",
   "s": 17.681,
   "e": 19.948
  },
  {
   "text": "The vessels fly open again,",
   "s": 20.564,
   "e": 21.825
  },
  {
   "text": "and the pressure spike trips the pain nerves around them.",
   "s": 22.249,
   "e": 24.678
  },
  {
   "text": "Here is the weird part.",
   "s": 25.459,
   "e": 26.268
  },
  {
   "text": "Those nerves report through the trigeminal nerve,",
   "s": 26.879,
   "e": 28.999
  },
  {
   "text": "the same cable that serves your forehead.",
   "s": 29.458,
   "e": 31.151
  },
  {
   "text": "So your brain gets the wires crossed,",
   "s": 31.82,
   "e": 33.406
  },
  {
   "text": "and feels the pain in your forehead instead of your mouth.",
   "s": 33.934,
   "e": 35.95
  },
  {
   "text": "Doctors call that referred pain.",
   "s": 36.712,
   "e": 38.281
  },
  {
   "text": "The fix is simple.",
   "s": 39.178,
   "e": 39.837
  },
  {
   "text": "Press your warm tongue to the roof of your mouth.",
   "s": 40.407,
   "e": 42.097
  },
  {
   "text": "The vessels calm down,",
   "s": 42.751,
   "e": 43.769
  },
  {
   "text": "the signal stops,",
   "s": 44.048,
   "e": 44.86
  },
  {
   "text": "and your brain goes back to guard duty.",
   "s": 45.246,
   "e": 46.835
  }
 ]
}